{"kind":"table","sheet":"Instructions","address":"A1:B16","rows":16,"cols":2,"values":[["Demand upload template",null],["Purpose","Prepare historical demand for Stockwise."],["Sample records","The first sheet contains 12 fictional monthly records. Replace ALL sample rows with your own data before forecasting."],["Keep the first sheet","Demand data must remain the first worksheet. The app reads only the first worksheet."],["Keep the headers","Row 1 must contain Date and Quantity. Do not add a title above the headers."],["Date","Enter a real Excel date, displayed as YYYY-MM-DD. Each row may be a transaction, daily total or monthly total."],["Quantity","Enter units as numbers of zero or more. Decimals are allowed. Do not enter currency values or text."],["Add records","Replace or extend rows beneath the headers. Do not add totals, notes or instruction rows to the data sheet."],["History","Linear Regression: 2+ months after differencing. ARIMA: 12+ months. SARIMA: 3+ seasons (36+ months at s = 12). Higher orders need more history. Use complete first and last months."],["Aggregation","The app adds quantities by month. Missing months count as zero. Do not mix transaction rows with overlapping monthly totals."],["Forecast","Choose Linear Regression, ARIMA or SARIMA, then Fit model. Each forecasts the next 12 months in demand units. Negative forecasts are capped at zero. The 12-row sample is too short for seasonal SARIMA."],["Upload","Save as .xlsx. Open Demand Forecasting and drop the file into the upload area, or use browse files. Limit: 5 MB and 50,000 records."],["Currency","This file contains unit quantities only. Select MYR or SGD for ordering and holding costs in the EOQ Calculator."],["Stationarity","Check & suggest stationarity tests ordinary/seasonal differencing with ADF and KPSS. Optional log(1 + demand) can help variance. Original records are preserved. Review the suggestion, then Fit model."],["Diagnostics and reports","Review R2, adjusted R2, named p-value tests and ACF/PACF. They describe model fit, not guaranteed accuracy. PDF reports include the selected model, transformations, diagnostics and charts."],["Local processing","The statistical engine downloads on first use and runs in your browser. Data is not uploaded for fitting. Accounts are local demos. Changing settings invalidates the forecast; refit before exporting."]]}
